.TH heliosctl 1 0.2.0 "heliosctl 0.2.0" "Helios Manual"
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
heliosctl \- The Helios Control API\*(Aqs command\-line client, for operators and AI agents
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBheliosctl\fR [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-\-endpoint\fR] [\fB\-\-profile\fR] [\fB\-\-region\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
The Helios Control API\*(Aqs command\-line client, for operators and AI agents (HLD 7.3.4.1). Requests are signed with your AWS credentials (an AWS profile that assumes helios\-operator). Every command takes \-\-json for one JSON document on stdout; errors then go to stderr as JSON, and the exit code says what happened: 0 done, 1 other, 2 invalid input, 3 not found, 4 refused, 5 timed out, 6 not authorized, 7 not reported yet, 8 throttled.
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Print one JSON document on stdout, and errors as JSON on stderr
.TP
\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fI<ENDPOINT>\fR
The Control API\*(Aqs base URL (…/dev)
.TP
\fB\-\-profile\fR \fI<PROFILE>\fR
The AWS profile: one that assumes helios\-operator [default: helios\-operator]
.TP
\fB\-\-region\fR \fI<REGION>\fR
The AWS region [default: the profile\*(Aqs]
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
heliosctl\-devices(1)
Devices in the bootstrap service
.TP
heliosctl\-streams(1)
A device\*(Aqs streams: list, get, start, stop, update, set\-destination
.TP
heliosctl\-inputs(1)
What a device can stream from
.TP
heliosctl\-profiles(1)
A device\*(Aqs encoding profiles
.TP
heliosctl\-location(1)
Where a device is: its GPS fix (or the last one), satellites and receivers. This is the device\*(Aqs exact position: keep it out of logs and anything shared
.TP
heliosctl\-wifi(1)
The Wi\-Fi networks a device joins: list, set, remove
.TP
heliosctl\-schema(1)
The Control API\*(Aqs operations, their inputs and outputs (OpenAPI), as JSON
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
\fB0\fR
Done (with \-\-wait: the device applied the change).
.TP
\fB1\fR
Anything else: a network error, an internal error, a response that doesn\*(Aqt parse.
.TP
\fB2\fR
Invalid input: a usage error, ValidationException, InvalidDestination, or a \-\-dry\-run that failed its checks.
.TP
\fB3\fR
Not found: DeviceNotFound, StreamNotFound.
.TP
\fB4\fR
Refused: SettingUnavailable, WifiNetworkRefused, or (with \-\-wait) the device rejected the change.
.TP
\fB5\fR
Timed out: DeviceUnreachable, or \-\-wait ran out of time (the device may still apply it).
.TP
\fB6\fR
Not authorized: no AWS credentials, or HTTP 403.
.TP
\fB7\fR
The device hasn\*(Aqt reported that yet: DeviceStateUnavailable.
.TP
\fB8\fR
Throttled: RateLimited, after retries.
With \-\-json, the error is one JSON document on standard error: {"error": {"type", "message", ...the error\*(Aqs members}}.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
\fBHELIOS_CONTROL_URL\fR
The Control API\*(Aqs base URL, as \-\-endpoint.
.TP
\fBAWS_PROFILE\fR
The AWS profile, as \-\-profile (default helios\-operator).
.TP
\fBAWS_REGION\fR
The AWS region, as \-\-region (default: the profile\*(Aqs).
.TP
\fBAWS_CONFIG_FILE, AWS_SHARED_CREDENTIALS_FILE\fR
Where the AWS SDK finds profiles and credentials.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/heliosctl/config.toml\fR
Settings, each used when its flag and environment variable aren\*(Aqt given: endpoint, profile and region. None of them is a secret.
.TP
\fI~/.aws/config\fR
The AWS profiles. The default profile, helios\-operator, should assume the helios\-operator role. The Rust AWS SDK can\*(Aqt read aws login sessions: give such a profile a credential_process of aws configure export\-credentials \-\-profile <profile> \-\-format process, and use it as helios\-operator\*(Aqs source_profile.
.SH SECURITY
heliosctl stores no credentials: requests are signed with SigV4 from the AWS credential chain. A Wi\-Fi passphrase is read only from \-\-passphrase\-file (or \- for standard input), and an SRT destination with a passphrase only from \-\-url\-file, never from an argument, so neither reaches shell history or the process list. Neither is ever printed: dry runs and output show ***.
.SH EXAMPLES
List devices:
.RS 4
\fBheliosctl devices list\fR
.RE
One device as JSON:
.RS 4
\fBheliosctl \-\-json devices get t\-01M80KAX049HNYQ4K9NYP8SNFH\fR
.RE
Check a change without sending it:
.RS 4
\fBheliosctl streams update d\-01M80KB9C9T0ZSPC64NZVY1QRA pocket \-\-bitrate 3000 \-\-dry\-run\fR
.RE
Start a stream and wait until it\*(Aqs applied:
.RS 4
\fBheliosctl streams start t\-01M80KAX049HNYQ4K9NYP8SNFH pocket \-\-wait\fR
.RE
Add a Wi\-Fi network, passphrase on standard input:
.RS 4
\fBheliosctl wifi set t\-01M80KAX049HNYQ4K9NYP8SNFH \-\-ssid Venue \-\-passphrase\-file \- < passphrase.txt\fR
.RE
An operation\*(Aqs input and output shapes:
.RS 4
\fBheliosctl schema SetWifiNetwork\fR
.RE
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
